d_7744_eacc90-ec_1\" data-label=\"Email\" type=\"email\" placeholder=\"\" value=\"\" data-type=\"email\" class=\"kb-field kb-text-style-field kb-email-field kb-field-1\" data-required=\"yes\"/></div><div class=\"kadence-blocks-form-field kb-form-field-2 kb-field-desk-width-100 kb-input-size-standard\"><label for=\"kb_field_7744_eacc90-ec_2\">Mobile Number<span class=\"required\">*</span></label><input name=\"kb_field_2\" id=\"kb_field_7744_eacc90-ec_2\" data-label=\"Mobile Number\" type=\"tel\" placeholder=\"\" value=\"\" data-type=\"tel\" class=\"kb-field kb-text-style-field kb-tel-field kb-field-2\" data-required=\"yes\"/></div><div class=\"kadence-blocks-form-field kb-form-field-3 kb-field-desk-width-100 kb-input-size-standard\"><label for=\"kb_field_7744_eacc90-ec_3\">Court to Appear in <span class=\"required\">*</span></label><input name=\"kb_field_3\" id=\"kb_field_7744_eacc90-ec_3\" data-label=\"Court to Appear in \" type=\"text\" placeholder=\"\" value=\"\" data-type=\"text\" class=\"kb-field kb-text-style-field kb-text-field kb-field-3\" data-required=\"yes\"/></div><div class=\"kadence-blocks-form-field kb-form-field-4 kb-field-desk-width-100 kb-input-size-standard\"><label for=\"kb_field_7744_eacc90-ec_4\">Case Related to<span class=\"required\">*</span></label><textarea name=\"kb_field_4\" id=\"kb_field_7744_eacc90-ec_4\" data-label=\"Case Related to\" type=\"textarea\" placeholder=\"\" data-type=\"textarea\" class=\"kb-field kb-text-style-field kb-textarea-field kb-field-4\" rows=\"1\" data-required=\"yes\"></textarea></div><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"_kb_form_id\" value=\"7744_eacc90-ec\"/><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"_kb_form_post_id\" value=\"7744\"/><input type=\"hidden\" name=\"action\" value=\"kb_process_ajax_submit\"/><label class=\"kadence-verify-label\">Email<input class=\"kadence-blocks-field verify\" type=\"text\" name=\"_kb_verify_email\" autocomplete=\"new-password\" aria-hidden=\"true\" placeholder=\"Email\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-1p-ignore=\"true\" data-lpignore=\"true\" /></label><div class=\"kadence-blocks-form-field kb-submit-field kb-field-desk-width-100\"><button class=\"kb-forms-submit button kb-button-size-standard kb-button-width-auto\">Connect me with a Attorney</button></div></form></div>\n<noscript><div class=\"kadence-blocks-form-message kadence-blocks-form-warning\">Please enable JavaScript in your browser to submit the form</div><style>.kadence-form-7744_eacc90-ec .kadence-blocks-form-field.kb-submit-field { display: none; }</style></noscript></div></div>\n\n</div></div></div></div>\n\n</div></div></div>\n</div>\n</div>\n\n\n\n<p>If you're facing legal issues in Harford County, Maryland, you'll likely end up at the Harford County Circuit Court. This court handles a range of cases, from civil disputes to criminal cases. In this article, we'll give you a comprehensive guide to the Harford County Circuit Court, including what it is, how it works, and what to expect if you find yourself there.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>What is the Harford County Circuit Court?</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Harford County Circuit Court is a trial court located in Bel Air, Maryland. It is one of Maryland's 24 circuit courts and is part of the Fifth Judicial Circuit, which also includes Anne Arundel, Carroll, and Howard counties. The court is presided over by five judges who are appointed by the governor and must be confirmed by the Maryland Senate.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>What cases are heard in the Harford County Circuit Court?</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Harford County Circuit Court hears a wide range of cases, including:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Civil cases: These cases involve disputes between individuals or organizations. Examples include contract disputes, personal injury cases, and family law cases such as divorce and child custody.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Criminal cases: The court handles both misdemeanor and felony criminal cases, including traffic offenses, drug offenses, and violent crimes.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Juvenile cases: The court has jurisdiction over cases involving minors, such as juvenile delinquency and child abuse and neglect cases.</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Appeals: The Harford County Circuit Court also hears appeals from the District Court and certain administrative agencies.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<h2>How does the Harford County Circuit Court work?</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Harford County Circuit Court operates much like any other court. When a case is filed, it is assigned to a judge who oversees the proceedings. Both parties are represented by attorneys who present evidence and argue their cases. Witnesses may be called to testify, and the judge ultimately makes a decision based on the evidence presented.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>What should I expect if I have a case in the Harford County Circuit Court?</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>If you have a case in the Harford County Circuit Court, it's important to be prepared. You'll likely need to hire an attorney, especially if the case is complex. You'll also need to gather evidence and be prepared to testify in court if necessary.</p>\n\n\n\n<p>During the trial, you'll need to follow the court's rules and procedures. This includes dressing appropriately, showing up on time, and addressing the judge respectfully. You'll also need to be prepared to listen carefully and respond to questions from the judge and the opposing party's attorney.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>How can I find more information about the Harford County Circuit Court?</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>If you need more information about the Harford County Circuit Court, you can visit the court's website at http://www.harfordcountymd.gov/195/Circuit-Court. The website has information about court procedures, forms, and fees. You can also contact the court directly at (410) 638-3426.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Harford County Circuit Court Case Search</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>If you're looking for information on a specific case in the Harford County Circuit Court, you can perform a case search using the Maryland Judiciary Case Search website. This website allows you to search for cases by party name, case number, or attorney name. You can also view a calendar of upcoming court dates.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Harford County Circuit Court Judges</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Harford County Circuit Court has three judges who preside over cases. These judges are:</p>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Angela M. Eaves</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Yolanda L. Curtin</li>\n\n\n\n<li>Kevin J. Mahoney</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<p>All three judges were appointed by the Governor of Maryland and confirmed by the Maryland Senate. They serve 15-year terms.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Harford County Circuit Court Address</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Harford County Circuit Court is located at 20 W. Courtland Street, Bel Air, MD 21014. The courthouse is open from 8:30 a.m. to 4:30 p.m. on weekdays, except for legal holidays.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Harford County District Court Clerk's Office</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>If you have a legal matter that falls under the jurisdiction of the Harford County District Court, you can contact the clerk's office for assistance. The clerk's office is located at 2 S. Bond Street, Bel Air, MD 21014. You can reach them by phone at (410) 638-3426.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Harford County Circuit Court Transcript Request</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>If you need a transcript of a court proceeding in the Harford County Circuit Court, you can request one from the court reporter who was present at the hearing. Contact information for court reporters can be obtained from the clerk's office.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Harford County Courthouse Marriage</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Harford County Circuit Court can also perform courthouse marriages. If you're interested in getting married at the courthouse, you should contact the clerk's office for more information.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Harford County District Court</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>In addition to the Harford County Circuit Court, there is also a Harford County District Court. The district court has jurisdiction over certain types of civil and criminal cases, including traffic violations, small claims, and misdemeanors. The district court is located at 2 S. Bond Street, Bel Air, MD 21014.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Harford County Court Jury Duty</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>If you are a resident of Harford County and are summoned for jury duty, you will be serving in either the Harford County Circuit Court or the Harford County District Court. Jury duty is an important civic duty and is essential for the proper functioning of the judicial system.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>Conclusion</h2>\n\n\n\n<p>The Harford County Circuit Court is an important part of Maryland's legal system. If you find yourself with a legal issue in Harford County, it's important to understand how the court works and what to expect. By hiring an experienced attorney and following the court's procedures, you can increase your chances of a successful outcome.</p>\n\n\n\n<h2>FAQs</h2>\n\n\n\n<ol>\n<li><strong>How do I file a case in the Harford County Circuit Court?</strong></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>To file a case in the Harford County Circuit Court, you'll need to fill out the appropriate forms and pay the required fees. You can find more information on the court's website or by contacting the court directly.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<ol start=\"2\">\n<li><strong>How long does it take for a case to be resolved in the Harford County Circuit Court?</strong></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>The length of time it takes for a case to be resolved in the Harford County Circuit Court can vary depending on the complexity of the case and the court's schedule. Some cases can be resolved in a matter of weeks or months, while others can take much longer.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<ol start=\"3\">\n<li><strong>Can I represent myself in the Harford County Circuit Court?</strong></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Yes, you have the right to represent yourself in court. However, it's generally recommended that you hire an experienced attorney, especially if your case is complex.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<ol start=\"4\">\n<li><strong>Can I appeal a decision made by the Harford County Circuit Court?</strong></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>Yes, you can appeal a decision made by the Harford County Circuit Court. The appeals process involves filing a notice of appeal and presenting your case to a higher court.</li>\n</ul>\n\n\n\n<ol start=\"5\">\n<li><strong>What should I do if I can't afford an attorney?</strong></li>\n</ol>\n\n\n\n<ul>\n<li>If you can't afford an attorney, you may be eligible for free or low-cost legal services. Contact the Harford County Circuit Court or a legal aid organization for more information.</li>\n</ul>\n",
